.TH "tangsible-revisit" "1" "2026-09-05" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-revisit - browse and reopen previous runs
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible revisit\fR [\fIplaybook.\&yml or role name\fR] [--tags | -t \fItags\fR] [--limit | -l \fIhosts\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBrevisit\fR lists every past invocation matching the specified arguments.\&
Selecting one replays its saved \fB.\&jsonl\fR event stream into a fresh tree —
the exact same live tree UI \fBtangsible-run\fR(1) uses, already frozen with
that run'\&s own final outcome, tags, and hosts.\&
.PP
With no arguments, every recorded run across every playbook and role is
shown.\& An optional \fIplaybook.\&yml\fR or \fIrole\fR argument narrows the list to
just that target; \fB--tags\fR/\fB-t\fR and \fB--limit\fR/\fB-l\fR narrow it further, to
runs whose own recorded tags/hosts overlap the given value.\&
.PP
Once a run is open, every normal live-tree key applies (see
\fBtangsible-run\fR(1)), including \fBr\fR to rerun it (starting a real, live
invocation from that point) and \fBd\fR to diff it against another recorded
run.\& 
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
The list was shown (and browsed, however briefly) and closed
normally with \fBq\fR/\fBCtrl-C\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
No recorded run matched the given filters, and the list was never
shown at all.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-run\fR(1), \fBtangsible-rerun\fR(1)
